{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310430-consuming-relics-and-apotheosis","id":310430,"title":"Consuming Relics and Apotheosis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-12T12:19:03-08:00","id":310430,"title":"Consuming Relics and Apotheosis","content":"Just a little question here, would an Arisen who achieved Apotheosis be able to consume a relic and increase its Sekhem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T14:41:48-08:00","id":310573,"title":"","content":"I would say no, at least for thematic reasons. Apotheosis lets you 'transfer' Sekhem, which apparently means you can create relics, which is on a whole different level than devouring Sekhem so that you can hang on to unlife for another day","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T20:23:31-08:00","id":310834,"title":"","content":"If I did allow it, and I'm pretty sure there's something that would prevent it, I'd make it a Memory 1 Sin. Of course, if they fail that roll, they get hurled into an immediate Death Cycle, likely lose any Sekhem they gained from the process, and afterwards have to deal with the fact that they sacrificed a portion of their &quot;real&quot; power trait for a taste of their old slavery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:38:27-08:00","id":310937,"title":"","content":"I explicitly wouldn't allow it. The point of Apotheosis is that you're giving away the power that comes with slavery in exchange for freedom, and the weakness and mortality that is part of the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 11-13-2014, 01:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T16:15:18-08:00","id":311712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310430-consuming-relics-and-apotheosis?p=310834#post310834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I did allow it, and I'm pretty sure there's something that would prevent it, I'd make it a Memory 1 Sin. Of course, if they fail that roll, they get hurled into an immediate Death Cycle, likely lose any Sekhem they gained from the process, and afterwards have to deal with the fact that they sacrificed a portion of their &quot;real&quot; power trait for a taste of their old slavery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just curious about the consequence tough. I guess that the idea of an instantaneous Death Cycle would be appropiate then. I guess that returned slavery would be impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}